# The "balanced" profile: NVFP4 only for the MLP projections, the checkpoint's FP8 for the GDN and attention
# projections, and the e4m3 head. The MLPs are 70 % of a verify's projection bytes, so this keeps most of the NVFP4
# speed while the GDN and attention layers keep the checkpoint's own weights. Everything else is ops/serve.env.
# The MLP overlay and the head are the published NVFP4 set's (the same files ops/serve.env loads).
#
# StairCut's verify prices come with serve.env: ops/stair-tables-nvfp4.json, measured on the full-NVFP4
# profile. The router corrects their level online (its per-class block factor, engine/lenrouter.py),
# but the staircase's shape for this profile is not measured, and neither is its speed on this release.
#
# Use it where a tool takes a profile (ops/gate.sh --profile ops/serve-balanced.env). docs/operations.md, "Profiles".
. "$(dirname "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")/serve.env"
NV=${HOME}/nvfp4-bf16/mlp.safetensors
HEAD=${HOME}/nvfp4-bf16/head-fp8.safetensors
